  "notes": "Deliberately scoped to half a catalogue, and the entry says so: \"only the uptempo half of this catalogue belongs here — the two-beat dance singles; the ballad half is radio country-pop and is not modelled in this section\". So `bpm` is the train-beat group's own band, the stated 136–186, with `mode` at 156 (\"Be My Baby Tonight\"); nothing from the 54–120 lane is encoded. Drums follow the stated split: \"at 152–186 a driven straight 8th stream with sticks, two-beat kick, hat on quarters, and a hard un-gated backbeat; the 136 cut adds a quarter kick and a hat opening on 4\" — which is `kick.densityPerBar` [2,4] on anchors 1 and 3, `hihat.base` \"4th\" with `openHat.pos` [\"4\"], and an accent tier at 106–127 for the un-gated backbeat. \"Fills confined to 8-bar boundaries\" is the parent's inherited 8/8 period, so `fills` is not authored. Harmony is the stated I–IV–V with V7 and the I–I7–IV turn on the modelled lane, the sevenths carried in `extensions`; the twelve-bar skeleton takes the lowest weight because the entry names the turn rather than a full blues catalogue. The melody follows \"warm baritone-tenor, mid-density, chorus built on a repeated chanted cell; ornament limited to a short scoop into sustained notes\". The dance cuts' \"extended instrumental outro\" is the 8–16 bar outro. ⚠ INFERRED: velocity tiers, `percs` contents, humanize and every melody, countermelody and bassline number. ⚠ The entry rates itself medium and its tempo readings carry [LOW-CONF] as a class; the ballad catalogue's deliberate omission is the entry's own decision, restated here so a later reader does not treat this model as the whole artist.",
